      "agent_input": "I'd like to review the Q3 2026 business report, please.",
      "agent_response": {
        "response": "Here's the **Meridian Analytics Q3 2026 Business Report** for your review:\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udccb Overview\n- **Period:** July 1 \u2013 September 7, 2026\n- **Prepared by:** Rachel Kim (VP of Sales) & Claire Fontaine (CFO)\n- **Distribution:** Executive Team\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udcca Executive Summary\nQ3 2026 was a strong quarter. The 15-person team closed **14 of 22 deals**, generating **$1,040,000** in new contract value. The pipeline remains healthy with several high-value deals still pending, and all critical support issues were resolved same-day.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udcb0 Sales Performance\n| Metric | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Total Closed Revenue | **$1,040,000** |\n| Top Region | **South \u2014 $468,000** |\n| Active Opportunities | 22 |\n| Deals Won | 14 |\n| Win Rate | **63.6%** (target: 55%) |\n| Pending Deals | ~$240,000 (3 deals, expected to close by end of Sept) |\n\nThe field sales team \u2014 **James Okafor, Sofia Delgado, and Marcus Webb** \u2014 drove all activity. Product mix shifted toward **Meridian Insights Pro** (majority of closed revenue), while **Meridian DataBridge** continues as a land-and-expand vehicle with upsell opportunities maturing in Q4.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83c\udf1f Key Highlights\n- **Top Deal:** Sofia Delgado closed a **$198,000** Meridian Insights Pro contract (Deal D019) on September 5.\n- **Headcount:** 15 employees across 5 departments \u2014 Sales (4), Engineering (5), Product (3), HR (1), Finance (2).\n- **Support SLA:** All critical tickets (TKT-004, TKT-011, TKT-015) resolved within 24 hours.\n- **License Utilization:** SKU-001 (Meridian Insights Pro) at **94% capacity** \u2014 procurement review scheduled for October.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udccc Next Steps\n1. Close pending deals **D007, D013, D020, D022** before Q3 end.\n2. Begin **Q4 pipeline review** \u2014 target **$1.2M** in new ARR.\n3. Resolve open support tickets **(TKT-013, TKT-016, TKT-019)** ahead of quarterly customer success calls.\n4. Conduct **license capacity review** for SKU-001 and SKU-003 in early October.\n5. HR to initiate **two new engineering hire approvals** with Kenji Obi to support the Q4 roadmap.\n\n---\n\n**Notable observation:** The \"Next Steps\" section lists *four* deal IDs (D007, D013, D020, D022) but the body text references only \"three pending deals.\" This may be a minor discrepancy worth flagging with the report authors.\n\nWould you like me to dig deeper into any of the supporting data (sales figures, expenses, support tickets, or employee details)?",
        "status_code": null
      },
